 {:seon.task/name "check-steps-are-tests-on-the-service"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: Tests; a helper can port the steps one by one from this plan. What exists, 2026-11-11: each bin/check step is an item of the test service already (seon.prove/plan-items :kind :step, its digest seon.proofs/step-digests, its bound the step-end factor times its median ms), but its body is bin/check --steps on a seeded store copy (seon.fx run-item), a runner of its own (about 320 lines) beside the service. Plan: each mode of seon.check that drives a root becomes a deftest whose root runs on a branch of the one seeded store (one store, many branches); only window and resume (what a store holds after a kill and reopen) keep a store file of their own, and lmdb-kill and lmdb-lock their envs. A ported step is then an ordinary test item, keyed by its reach like any test, and leaves check-steps. Removes, once the last is ported: bin/check's runner and its per-step store copies, store-steps!, seon.proofs/check-steps. Order: the cheapest first (config, system, mcp, agent-checks). Proof per step: its deftest red under the mutation its step names, green on main."
